// Canonical combining class, as 393 (lo, hi, class) runs covering the 934
// code points whose class is not zero. Everything absent is class 0.
//
// This is the key to canonical ordering: when several marks follow one
// base character, normalization sorts them by this number, so that a
// Persian word written with its harakat in one order compares equal to
// the same word with them typed in another. Marks of class 0, and any
// two marks of equal class, are never reordered relative to each other.
